{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1743,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Marco Polo wrote that the Khan's letters raced two hundred miles in a day. Yet no single horse made the trip.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 161
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "His riders went bound in tight bands, their belts jingling with bells.",
   "from": 165,
   "to": 281
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But a horse at full gallop tires long before sunset.",
   "from": 285,
   "to": 364
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So every twenty-five miles, the Khan built a station called a Yam.",
   "from": 368,
   "to": 486
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Some kept four hundred horses, half saddled, half out at grass.",
   "from": 489,
   "to": 593
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Polo counted over ten thousand stations and three hundred thousand horses.",
   "from": 596,
   "to": 723
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And who supplied all those horses? The villages next door.",
   "from": 726,
   "to": 821
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "villager",
   "text": "Four hundred horses? I have three goats!",
   "from": 825,
   "to": 918
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Every rider also carried a paiza, a metal tablet with a falcon.",
   "from": 921,
   "to": 1012
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "If his horse broke down, anyone he met had to hand over theirs.",
   "from": 1016,
   "to": 1103
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "merchant",
   "text": "Hey! That's my horse!",
   "from": 1107,
   "to": 1153
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, no horse ran far. Only the letter did.",
   "from": 1168,
   "to": 1255
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The bells rang out long before the rider arrived.",
   "from": 1259,
   "to": 1323
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the next station saddled a fresh horse, and a clerk wrote down the time.",
   "from": 1327,
   "to": 1444
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The letter changed hands at a gallop and never stopped.",
   "from": 1448,
   "to": 1515
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Fruit picked one morning in the capital reached the Khan the next evening, ten days' journey away.",
   "from": 1518,
   "to": 1641
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Every horse got tired. The letter never did.",
   "from": 1645,
   "to": 1719
  }
 ],
